    <statement><p>Find the derivative of the function
<m>y(x) = m^x + x^m</m>.
Assume that <m>m</m> is a positive constant.</p>
<p><m>y'(x) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>m^{x}\ln\mathopen{}\left(m\right)+mx^{m-1}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>y'(x) = (m^x) \ln(m) + m x^{m - 1}</me>


</solution>
